Subject: [STATSGRASS] grass 61/R kriging and splining
Message-ID: <5B6C8A16-7A6A-479A-93FE-A8D534B7ABB6@umn.edu>

I just read Roger and Markus's paper "Open Source geocomputation:  
using the R data analysis language integrated with GRASS GIS and  
PostgreSQL data base systems"  with great interest, as I was looking  
for kriging and splining examples with GRASS and R, and I have just  
moved my databases over to  PostgreSQL.

There was a reference to document updates in the introduction that  
may be available on the Hannover site (however I was not able to find  
anything). Are there any more recent versions of this paper  
(particularly that address GRASS 6.1 differences). As an alternative,  
is anyone aware of other kriging or splining examples (I have read  
the GRASS / R interface article that appeared in vol. 3 of the GRASS  
news letter) ?

If not, that's ok... I'll continue to muddle forward. But if there  
are some additional documented kriging and splining examples  
performed on GRASS 6.1, I would love to see them.

As always, thanks for the thoughts.

Kirk


